tree-sitter-ral
===============

A tree-sitter grammar for the ral shell language, used for editor
syntax highlighting via queries/highlights.scm.

The canonical source is grammar.js. Everything tree-sitter derives
from it is generated, not tracked: src/parser.c, src/grammar.json,
src/node-types.json, and the runtime headers under src/tree_sitter/
(parser.h, alloc.h, array.h). The compiled parser library (ral.dylib
and friends) and the node-gyp build/ tree are likewise build outputs.
All of these are listed in .gitignore.

Regeneration
------------

The package.json build script runs the generate step:

    npm run build        # tree-sitter generate && node-gyp build

or, to produce only the parser sources without compiling:

    tree-sitter generate

Run this after editing grammar.js to refresh src/parser.c and the
accompanying JSON and headers. Without node installed, evaluate
grammar.js with the CLI's own JS engine instead:

    tree-sitter generate --js-runtime native

Test the grammar against the corpus in test/corpus with
`tree-sitter test` (npm test).
